{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED for exact head d3131e2f48db939f5fa4df2d57a3bb5826b3a8f4.\n\n1. The actor response is no longer bounded in the dimension this repair adds. digestStatus (digest.go:253-263) and digestWait (346-355) append every stale, reneged, and cancelled commitment involving the actor, forever and without a cap or skipped count. A long-lived actor with many terminal commitments therefore gets O(terminal history) status and every wait response, contrary to Task 3's bounded-response condition and the test's own claim that growth is logarithmic. TestStatusDigestIsActorOrientedAndBounded only scales unrelated decision padding while keeping commitment cardinality fixed, so it passes while this regression remains. Bound/summarize the historical terminal set or make wait select only state transitions after the cursor, with a scaled terminal-history fixture.\n\n2. The new wait assertion still does not prove the transition it claims. digest_test.go:287-303 sets the requested frontier to the current depth, manually appends commitments without their causal decisions, and then asserts that all current terminal rows appear. That proves a full current-state echo, not that a commitment which became stale/reneged after the cursor is delivered. Build this case through the fold (or at least append the actual retiring decisions and advance from a prior snapshot) so a broken cursor cut cannot pass.\n\n3. The exact head is not gofmt-clean: gofmt -d changes the waitDelta field alignment at digest.go:112-120.\n\nThe involvement predicate does correctly recover both parties for the fold's reachable cancelled/reneged shapes, and wait's act join correctly supplies actor/kind/target for ratify and supersede. Passed: make vet, make test, make race, make build, and git diff --check; worktree remained clean.","body":{"head":"d3131e2f48db939f5fa4df2d57a3bb5826b3a8f4","tests":"make vet; make test; make race; make build; git diff --check; gofmt -d (non-empty)","verdict":"changes-requested"}}